cmprovision4 (2.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Several switches on the stand. Settings → Ethernet switches lists them,
    each with its own address and SNMP read and write access; Add switch
    and Edit open one at a time. Test and Save read what the switch calls
    itself and its base MAC, so one switch is not added twice under two
    addresses. The 2.3 switch settings become the first switch of the list
    and stay in place for going back to 2.3.
  * A module's board is "hostname port": the switch's sysName before the
    first dot, then the port's description or name, with one switch too.
    The module keeps its switch and port apart as well: the webhook's JSON
    has "switch" and "port" next to "board", and labels may print $switch
    and $port.
  * The board comes from one map of the whole stand: every switch is read,
    a port that leads to another switch of the stand (it shows that
    switch's own MAC: base MAC, interface MACs, its address in the
    provisioner's ARP cache) is a link and never a module's port, and each
    module belongs to one port. A link found before holds while the switch
    behind it is silent.
  * The Ports page draws a block for each switch with its line inside:
    hostname, serial, base MAC, address, model, when it was polled and its
    PoE draw. A silent switch keeps its last snapshot and says since when
    it is silent; two switches with one name are warned about; a link
    shows → and where it leads.
  * PoE restart works switch by switch: each has its own lock and write
    access, a silent switch skips only its own ports, and the messages,
    the module log and the outage banner name ports "hostname port". Power
    on goes through the switch of the outage. The dashboard offers Restart
    by the module's switch and lists up to 100 modules.
  * A switch that did not answer is asked again after 30 seconds, not on
    every page refresh and module start. A module start gets no board from
    the last snapshot of a switch that does not answer now: the module may
    be elsewhere, and the log says where and when it was last seen.
  * One switch added under two addresses (its IP and its name) is drawn
    once; the Ports page and Settings say to delete one of them.
  * The upgrade from a version before 2.4 takes a snapshot first, as the
    upgrade to 2.0 does: cmprovision-restore goes back to 2.3.

