cmprovision4 (2.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Self-signed certificates for Mattermost and webhooks: a Mattermost bot,
    Mattermost webhook or JSON webhook channel can trust its server's own
    certificate. Fetch from the server takes the certificates the server
    presents and shows their names, validity and SHA-256 fingerprints; the
    channel then trusts them besides the system's CAs and still checks the
    host name. A certificate counts only for the server it was saved with.
    Accept any certificate (insecure) turns the check off and is marked in
    the list of channels.
  * A certificate error of a channel, its Test button or the channel lookup
    says what to do instead of a bare cURL error 60: fetch the certificate,
    put the name it was issued for in the address, or check the clock when
    it has expired.
  * Telegram errors on the settings page no longer show the bot token, which
    Guzzle puts in the URL of its error messages.
  * The package depends on php-curl, which hands the trusted certificates
    to curl.

