cmprovision4 (1.6.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: postinst never follows symlinks in places the web user can
    write to. Since 1.6.5 a compromised web process could put a symlink in
    place of storage/app/upload-tmp and be handed its target, any root-owned
    directory, on the next package upgrade.
  * Security: stored secrets (Mattermost bot token, SNMP community, SNMPv3
    passwords) are only used for the address they were saved with; a new
    address needs them entered again.
  * The code belongs to root; the web server writes only to storage,
    bootstrap/cache, public/uploads, etc, the database directory and .env.
    Existing installations are converted on upgrade.
  * Dashboard: the log refreshes itself, shows the date of older entries and
    names the time zone.
  * Message boxes are in colour again (CSS rebuilt, Tailwind 1 leftovers
    replaced); the browser tab shows an icon.
  * Packaging: debhelper compat 13; services are restarted after an upgrade
    instead of being stopped before it.

