cmprovision4 (1.6.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * EEPROM firmware download works again: images come from the
    firmware-2711 default/latest channels on GitHub (only missing files,
    checksum verified) and from the rpi-eeprom package; new artisan
    command firmware:update. (upstream #43)
  * Image upload shows progress, speed and remaining time, can be
    cancelled and reports errors; the Images page refreshes itself while
    the SHA256 is being computed.
  * Image write failures are explained in the web log (curl exit code,
    decompressor errors, diagnosis); nginx no longer drops slow downloads
    (send_timeout 6h for /uploads/, added to existing installations);
    a failed write clears the partition table so the module net-boots
    again; module reports are retried for up to 10 minutes instead of
    being lost. (upstream #59, #44)
  * /scriptexecute never answers with an error page: an unreachable SNMP
    switch, internal errors and a deleted project go to the web log.
  * Project activation (EEPROM image build) is shared by the web UI and
    the API, with settings normalised and the firmware path allowlisted.
  * Settings: deleting a static IP updates dnsmasq.conf; hostnames are
    written correctly.
  * Images page tolerates missing files; timestamps shown in the server's
    time zone (storage stays UTC); upload_tmp_dir kept on disk (Debian 13
    has /tmp in RAM); production defaults in .env; [pi4] in config.txt so
    EEPROM flashing also works on a Pi 4. (upstream #24, #40, #41)
  * Upgrades restart php-fpm, so opcache does not keep serving the code of
    the previous version.
  * API: project scripts readable and changeable, script CRUD. (#55)
  * Ships public/uploads (#28) and the cmprovision-backup /
    cmprovision-restore commands; phpunit is no longer installed on the
    server (it was a production dependency);
    Docker test bench; README for NetworkManager-based Raspberry Pi OS.

